 "ideas": [
  {
   "id": 1,
   "title": "Price floor: only buy 95c and above (the pocket that pays)",
   "why": "In the feed the 95-97c and 97-99c buckets are +$137 and +$69 (hit rate 1-1.7 points above price), while 90-95c is -$248. The floor is chosen after seeing the result, so it must be proven forward.",
   "how_to_test": "Paper-log every candidate the bot sees (price, side, asset, strategy, result) with a pre-registered rule 'price >= 0.95'. Judge on win rate minus (price + fee) with a Wilson interval; the feed's 40-trade window is too short, so ask the VM chat for a one-off CSV of `orders` (ts, ticker, side, book, filled, avg_price, pnl).",
   "n_needed": 600
  },
  {
   "id": 2,
   "title": "Maker-side entries (post a resting limit one cent better)",
   "why": "Fees are about $73 of the $62.8 loss: gross edge is about zero, the toll is the loss. The maker fee is about a quarter of the taker fee (0.0175 vs 0.07 x C x P x (1-P)), which would cut the toll to about $18. Risk: you only get filled when price moves against you.",
   "how_to_test": "Paper: for each real signal record the bid/ask at signal time, post a virtual limit at the bid+1c and count a fill only when trades print through it; compare fill rate and the win rate of FILLED versus all signals (adverse selection).",
   "n_needed": 300
  },
  {
   "id": 3,
   "title": "Distance-to-strike / volatility filter for the hourly BTC late favourite",
   "why": "The 3 late-favourite losses are 'BTC crossed the strike in the last minutes'. The ticker holds the strike and the trade time, so the distance in volatility units (|spot - strike| / (sigma x sqrt(minutes left))) is computable from free public spot candles.",
   "how_to_test": "Join the trade list with public 1-minute BTC spot candles (any free exchange feed, not Kalshi). Bucket trades by z-distance, check whether the three losses sit in the lowest bucket, then paper a minimum-z rule.",
   "n_needed": 400
  },
  {
